The field report behind the VS Code `--call` door, FROZEN at one commit. It is the guide file docs/using-reflow2-in-vscode-without-mcp.md as it stands at 2b95bb4 on reflow2 branch feat/vscode-call-door (187 lines; Anthony, work machine, sessions of 2026-10-01 and 02). A byte-identical copy is kept, as field reports are, in the git-ignored docs/feedback/ (dec:field-reports-are-untracked-because-the-repository-is-public), so the location resolves in any checkout on this machine. The checksum is the same. The guide on the branch is the living copy and will move on; this node is the dated snapshot the triage reads. It supersedes the 12-limitation version recorded as fact:field-report-vscode-copilot-with-mcp-blocked-reaches-reflow2-only-through-the-call-door-2026-10-01 (using_call.md at 9b49869).

The location first named the branch file ("…@feat/vscode-call-door 2b95bb4"). reconcile_artifacts read that as a missing file, so it was moved here the same day.

WHAT IT HOLDS:
- "Where reflow2 stands" (the planned order for the door);
- what works today with no change, and a MEASURED table of 10 rows;
- working patterns, and VS Code agent hooks (1.138);
- 20 limitations, 10 tool frictions and 19 ideas.

KNOWN DEFECT IN THE SNAPSHOT: limitation 16's first line or lines are lost. Line 120 holds only "don't run the door in such a folder." The "Where reflow2 stands" list names limitation 16 as "a one-shot call never creates a design in a folder that names one on a server", which matches fact:a-cli-call-in-a-pointer-folder-mints-a-fresh-local-store-2026-10-01.

The report's own conclusions are claims to test, not facts. Registered and PARKED under dec:a-dated-field-report-is-registered-and-parked. Triaged under rule:field-feedback-issues-are-root-caused-and-ideas-are-brainstormed on Anthony's word ("Full triage, 4 agents", 2026-10-02), split four ways:
- the door, sessions and export;
- finding tools and argument shapes;
- write safety;
- the VS Code setup itself.
Every finding names this node as its `source`.
